accessWidener	v2	named

# Compress 'em registers two creative tabs and fills them through
# CreativeModeTab.Builder#displayItems(...).
#
# 26.1 made CreativeModeTab$Output protected. DisplayItemsGenerator's only
# method takes an Output parameter, so once Output is inaccessible the interface
# cannot be implemented outside vanilla at all: javac rejects both an explicit
# parameter type and a lambda whose type would have to be inferred. Vanilla is
# unaffected because it builds its own tabs inside net.minecraft.world.item,
# where "protected" also grants package access -- which is exactly why this is
# easy to miss and only shows up when compiling a mod.
#
# There is no alternative route: Item.Properties has no tab(...) on either
# loader, and 26.1 adds no tab-content registry.
#
# 1.21.11 declares Output public, so this entry is a no-op there. The two files
# cannot be merged: 26.1 rejects the named namespace outright, and the header line
# has to agree with the target's mapping channel. Prism turns whichever file is
# configured into the NeoForge access transformer automatically.
accessible	class	net/minecraft/world/item/CreativeModeTab$Output
